===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ja|振り仮名|tr=furigana|t=annotating kana|lit=assigned phonetic character}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|furigana}}

# {{lb|en|Japanese|_|typography}} [[kana|Kana]] printed next to or above a [[kanji]] or other [[character]] to indicate the [[pronunciation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Insup Taylor; M. Martin Taylor|title=Writing and Literacy in Chinese, Korean and Japanese|publisher=John Benjamins|edition=revised|isbn=9789027269447|page=290|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qaK2BQAAQBAJ&pg=PA290&dq=%22furigana%22&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22furigana%22&f=false|text='''Furigana''' are indispensable for some names of people and places whose Kanji are not included among the official Kanji list, and whose sounds can be unusual and even idiosyncratic.}}

